slices.description:
Migration 0007 (§9.1): users.organizer, organizer_blocked_at, organizer_trusted_at/_by; profiles.owner_user_id with a non-unique index, profiles.rev; clubs.verified, created_by, created_at, merged_into and the 'unaffiliated' club row; tournaments.created_at, hidden_by, hidden_from, hide_reason, self_entry, rev; app_meta.staff_rev (set to revision); the entry_withdrawals table; floor including member clubs and merged clubs.

Repository (§4.3):
- load and rows read and write the new columns, and rows() fills in missing keys so install.php and seed-athletes.php keep working;
- rows() skips members; transaction($fn,$actor) injects the actor; read-only organizers and flags maps;
- persist() uses plain INSERT for new keys and UPDATE…WHERE for existing ones, maps 1062 to 409, deletes profiles missing from the result after entries and draws (throwing if rowCount is 0), and writes stamps and withdrawal tombstones;
- organizerSnapshot($userId,$today), profileRow(), and a guestTournaments join for community/trusted and the current club name and verified state.

Domain and workspace.js parity:
- helpers organizer, staffIds, staffProfile, community, trusted, manages, managesProfile(u,a,db?), outsideEntry, canEnter(u,t,db?), canCreateTournament;
- Domain::stale plus central stamping in execute (§5.8);
- the publicData visibility matrix (§5.2) with the hidden-tournament self-entry rule;
- changes to tournament.save, profile.save, profile.archive, entry.save (editor in community tournaments, identity kept on self-entries, club override) and entry.remove (owner branch first, tombstones);
- new commands profile.forget, athlete.save, athlete.archive, athlete.forget, entry.self (drawn-category and minor/trust gates), club.save, club.merge, club.adopt, tournament.hide (reason, hiddenFrom, withdrawSelf);
- PHP-only forgetMember, forgetProfile, detach and retain; pure athleteFields;
- constants per §5.4; CONTACT pattern with shared test cases; unified 404 literals for member actors.

Other PHP and JS:
- Clubs.php: key() and pick() (pure; pending club name when quotas are used up);
- Actors::of;
- Settings.php stub: effective() computes the derived keys from the config only;
- Rules::sameClub, used in makeDraw;
- GuestView: sparse community/trusted fields, upcoming() excludes untrusted community tournaments, bracket slots keep {initials, club} with club null for unverified and '' for unaffiliated, summary.clubs skips unaffiliated, and new public categoryList() and bracket();
- JS mirrors in workspace.js, engine.js (makeDraw, clubConflicts, fingerprintCounts), guest-view.js and profile-data.js (clubKey);
- initialWorkspace: unaffiliated club, verified flags, staffRev:1, demo-organizer and demo-athlete accounts and profile, selfEntry:true on t-winter-2027.

i18n and tests: register every new dictionary in i18n.js and in the exact DICTIONARY_SOURCES list; add athlete-view.js and athlete-data.js to NOT_UI; extend the xss-scan scope to future modules; fill server-domain-en.js; parity, unit and HTTP tests per §12.

index.php:
- Settings::effective right after the PDO opens;
- bootstrap for a member organizer: step-up check, organizerSnapshot plus publicData(Actors::of), the ?t&rev unchanged short-circuit, 1500/h per session with unchanged answers not counted;
- command for a member: ORGANIZER_TYPES, step-up, 60/min and 1200/h per account, global member-tx bucket of 120/min, 402, transaction with the actor and flags; account_audit after tournament.hide, club.*, profile.forget;
- account.password forbidden for members.

Auth: ws {at,last} set in enter(); 401 code 'reauth' after 30 min idle or 12 h; organizer-unlock using the login limits.

Members:
- signup with roles and athlete: validation before any transaction (Domain::athleteFields, Clubs::pick on clubs read-only), then one Members::tx for user, profile, billing (free-signup marker), new club (plain INSERT; on 1062 re-read the club) and the profiles row via Repository::profileRow; organizer-enable-ip-day 3 per /64; duplicate-e-mail limit 5/h per /64 that gives 429 for every outcome;
- adminAction create in free mode marks free-signup;
- new actions organizer (block, hideTournaments with withdrawSelf), organizer-trust, organizer-bulk (up to 50, done/failed); adminList filters organizers, organizers-pending, athletes, free-signup and ownerOf;
- erase calls Repository::transaction with Domain::forgetMember after confirmEnd and Stripe deletion, before the member transaction.

Routes: roles route (10/h, block 403, running tournaments 409); me with caps, athletes, signupMode, selfEntry and pendingOrganizers for the Admin; public-config fields.

Chat: the lobby skips untrusted community tournaments except the viewer's own; o:2 for an untrusted organizer.

Jobs: jobs/accounts.php gets NOT EXISTS conditions for profiles, tournaments and clubs; jobs/community.php runs community-retention through Domain::retain, calling effective first.

- app.js:
  - communityOnly(user) in shell, render, #screen polling and rerenderLanguage; #screen polls through Client.bootstrap({t,rev}) and ignores unchanged answers;
  - handleError: a 401 with reauth opens a password modal, calls organizer-unlock and retries once;
  - tournamentsPage: first-run card, Admin/editor filter (all/staff/community/hidden), optgroup select, badges, 'Kopiuj link do zapisów', data-tournament-admin mount;
  - tournamentForm: organizer defaults to open with selfEntry, new note text, hidden banner with the reason;
  - profileForm with club-picker and guardian consent for members under 16; checkModal club field for self-entries with a warning that the draw will be dropped; entryForm privacy notice in community tournaments; club display from clubName(clubId) or the snapshot;
  - ui.bracket(publicCategory,{highlight}) returning SafeHtml; data-athlete-cta mount in guestPage; imports of athlete-boot.js and settings-boot.js (created empty); demo buttons for organizer and athlete.
- registry: defaultPage(role,user), visible(user) in allows and navItems. me.js: demoMe with caps and athletes.
- client.js: bootstrap parameters and an idempotent upgrade of a stored demo (unaffiliated club, verified, selfEntry, rev, staffRev, demo member accounts).
- club-picker.js: radio group plus an ARIA 1.2 combobox, or a native select below 300 clubs, with a 'Czy chodzi o…?' match.
- chat.js renders o:2 as 'Organizator (społeczność)'; chat-boot.js adds the member role to event-chat.
- index.html links athlete.css and settings.css.
- EN keys go to organizer-en.js.

- Contract tests between same-wave slices: effective config inside RouteContext and the account/athlete routes; Actors::of; transaction with an actor; organizerSnapshot; Clubs::pick in signup.
- Browser scenarios from §12 on phone and desktop, PL and EN.
- Performance budget at 5,000 profiles and 200 tournaments (load < 400 ms, organizerSnapshot < 50 ms, unchanged bootstrap < 20 ms).
- Walk the §11 checklist item by item with evidence.
- Seam fixes in any file, each listed in the commit message.
- Documentation:
  - README: roles, visibility matrix, trusting organizers;
  - INSTALL-PL: signup_force_off, app_settings, the new seed-athletes behaviour;
  - DEPLOY-PL: §3.3 matrix, abuse procedure (pause, bulk block), 0007 floor;
  - HANDOFF: state and §15 questions;
  - VALIDATION: results and the budget.
